{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787151752,"nonce":"PPwnsTFXw7GMGZ2bj9m1L8c8yZ4=","message":"**A second consequence of the same missing validation, found by a red team after this ticket was filed: an unvalidated `base_url` does not only go EMPTY, it can go MALFORMED.**\n\n`link()` (`internal/channels/render/slack/text.go:127-132`) escapes the label and **not the URL**: it returns `\"\u003c\" + url + \"|\" + escape(label) + \"\u003e\"`. `Links.Group` is `v.baseURL + \"/groups/\" + \u003cuuid\u003e` (`view.go:533`), and the UUID half is structurally safe — `uuid.UUID.String()` can only produce canonical hex. **The `baseURL` half is operator input with no validation at all**, which is this ticket. So every mrkdwn metacharacter reaches the payload verbatim. Observed, with the value fed and the string rendered:\n\n- `OTO_HTTP_BASE_URL=\"http://x|y\"` → `\u003chttp://x|y/groups/\u003cuuid\u003e|open in oto\u003e` — **two `|` inside one link tag.** Slack takes the first as the URL/label separator, so the label becomes `y/groups/\u003cuuid\u003e|open in oto`.\n- `base_url` containing `\u003e` → the `\u003e` closes the link tag early and everything after it, including the label, falls out as literal text.\n- `base_url` containing `\u003c` → a second unescaped `\u003c` in the payload; the markup is ambiguous.\n- `base_url` containing a newline → a raw `\\n` inside the `\u003curl|label\u003e` span.\n\n⚠️ **`link()` is not the thing to fix.** Eleven call sites hand it a URL oto built itself, and every one of them is safe for the same reason: `baseURL` plus a UUID, or an Alertmanager/Grafana URL oto assembled. Escaping the URL inside `link()` would be belt-and-braces, but it would also silently mangle a legitimately percent-encoded query string, and the Alertmanager silence deep link is exactly that (`view.go`'s `AlertmanagerSilenceNew`, full of `%7B`/`%22`). **The single check that fixes all of these is the one this ticket asks for: refuse a `base_url` that is not a well-formed absolute URL with a scheme and a host.** That is also why the scheme-shape question in **Scope** above is not a nicety — `url.Parse` accepting `\"oto.example.com\"` is the same hole.\n\n⭐ **And it raises the priority of the shape check over the mere non-empty check.** An empty `base_url` produces a card with no links, which is bad and visible. A `base_url` with a `\u003e` in it produces a card whose text is silently wrong for every reader, which is worse and invisible — nothing errors, nothing logs, and the card still ships.\n\n**A third consequence has its own ticket: `1cd496f`.** The same unbounded `base_url` also breaks Slack section truncation, because `truncateSection`'s `… \u003cURL|see full detail in oto\u003e` suffix costs `len(URL) + 29` against a fixed 100-byte allowance. Any oto deep link over **71 bytes** makes the function that enforces the 3 000-character limit return more than 3 000, and `Validate`'s V5 check then refuses the whole delivery. The shipped default leaves 4 bytes of headroom. That one is a real bug in `truncateAt` regardless of validation and is filed separately — but a `base_url` length bound would also stop it, which is worth knowing when choosing how strict this check should be.","files":null}]}